a step and falls off the stage.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:01.734
[ Clapping ]
"You got this, Becky!"

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:03.868
[ Clattering ]

00:08:03.868 --> 00:08:06.300
[ Thudding ]

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:11.834
[ Clattering, thudding ]

00:08:11.834 --> 00:08:13.601
[ Clattering, thudding ]
[ Laughter ]

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:15.601
[ Clattering, thudding ]

00:08:15.601 --> 00:08:17.234
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.234 --> 00:08:23.267
[ Clattering, thudding ]

00:08:23.267 --> 00:08:26.200
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.934 --> 00:08:30.334
[ Clapping ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:30.334 --> 00:08:32.167
Now, this new billionaire tax

00:08:32.167 --> 00:08:36.033
would essentially be a tax,
in part, on unrealized gains

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:38.801
on things like stocks you own,
but haven't sold yet.

00:08:38.801 --> 00:08:40.767
It may sound a little
complicated, but don't worry.

00:08:40.767 --> 00:08:43.100
CBS News has hired
a very knowledgeable

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:45.667
